<sheets>
<sheet name="">
<description>USB-C, protection and USB-UART</description>
<plain>
<wire x1="7.62" y1="25.4" x2="116.84" y2="25.4" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="116.84" y1="25.4" x2="116.84" y2="180.34" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="116.84" y1="180.34" x2="7.62" y2="180.34" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="7.62" y1="180.34" x2="7.62" y2="25.4" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<text x="8.89" y="176.53" size="2.54" layer="97">USB-C SINK / ESD / VBUS PROTECTION</text>
<wire x1="119.38" y1="25.4" x2="271.78" y2="25.4" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="271.78" y1="25.4" x2="271.78" y2="180.34" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="271.78" y1="180.34" x2="119.38" y2="180.34" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="119.38" y1="180.34" x2="119.38" y2="25.4" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<text x="120.65" y="176.53" size="2.54" layer="97">NATIVE USB TO ESP32-S3 GPIO19 / GPIO20</text>
<text x="10.16" y="43.18" size="1.778" layer="97">CC1 and CC2 each have 5.1k Rd. USB-C sink/UFP, 5V, no Power Delivery.</text>
<text x="10.16" y="38.1" size="1.778" layer="97">R3 joins shell to GND; C2 is optional, not fitted. F1 protects against sustained overcurrent.</text>
<text x="10.16" y="33.02" size="1.778" layer="97">VBUS input capacitance: C1 0.1u + C6 4.7u + C7 0.1u = 4.9u nominal.</text>
<text x="121.92" y="43.18" size="1.778" layer="97">D1 at connector. R4/R5 at module. Route both USB segments as 90-ohm differential pairs.</text>
<text x="121.92" y="38.1" size="1.778" layer="97">ESP GPIO19=D-, GPIO20=D+. Native USB supports flashing and host data; UART pads provide recovery.</text>
<text x="121.92" y="33.02" size="1.778" layer="97">Firmware must advertise its USB power requirement and hold RF off until USB configuration.</text>
</plain>
