<text x="8.89" y="176.53" size="2.54" layer="97">5V -&gt; 3V3 BUCK (TLV62569, 1.5 MHz, 2 A)</text>
<wire x1="165.1" y1="25.4" x2="271.78" y2="25.4" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="271.78" y1="25.4" x2="271.78" y2="180.34" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="271.78" y1="180.34" x2="165.1" y2="180.34" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="165.1" y1="180.34" x2="165.1" y2="25.4" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<text x="166.37" y="176.53" size="2.54" layer="97">FILTERED RF RAILS</text>
<text x="10.16" y="43.18" size="1.778" layer="97">VOUT = 0.6 V x (1 + 453k/100k) = 3.32 V. L = 2.2 uH, COUT = 22 uF (TI DS Table 4 'checked' combination), CFF = 6.8 pF (TI 8.2.2.2).</text>
<text x="10.16" y="38.1" size="1.778" layer="97">Budget: S3 350mA + RF/LED 170mA = 520mA at 3.32V; at 4.75V / 85% efficiency, USB input ~428mA. RF duty limits apply.</text>
<text x="10.16" y="33.02" size="1.778" layer="97">Place U2/L1 at the USB end; keep BUCK_SW copper minimal and away from RF section.</text>
<text x="167.64" y="43.18" size="1.778" layer="97">3V3_RADIO: SX1280 only.  3V3_PA: RFX2401C only (TX ~90-120 mA pulses).</text>
<text x="167.64" y="38.1" size="1.778" layer="97">Separate beads keep PA current steps off the transceiver and buck noise off both.</text>
</plain>
