<text x="8.89" y="176.53" size="2.54" layer="97">BOOT / STATUS / ROLE AT RESET</text>
<wire x1="134.62" y1="25.4" x2="271.78" y2="25.4" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="271.78" y1="25.4" x2="271.78" y2="180.34" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="271.78" y1="180.34" x2="134.62" y2="180.34" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<wire x1="134.62" y1="180.34" x2="134.62" y2="25.4" width="0.3048" layer="97" style="shortdash"/>
<text x="135.89" y="176.53" size="2.54" layer="97">BOTTOM-SIDE GPIO / UART / JTAG / TEST PADS</text>
<text x="10.16" y="43.18" size="1.778" layer="97">SW2 low=TX, high=RX. Sample only at reset; firmware changes role after reboot. RX is the open-switch default.</text>
<text x="10.16" y="38.1" size="1.778" layer="97">J5 GPIO35/36/37/38 are 3.3V bidirectional GPIO on this S3 N8 module. Headers are not 5V tolerant.</text>
<text x="10.16" y="33.02" size="1.778" layer="97">BOOT/BIND on GPIO0. Reset via TP1. USB flashing is normal; UART0 pads provide recovery.</text>
<text x="134.62" y="100.33" size="1.27" layer="97">J3: 3.3V logic. 5V is USB output after F1; do not backfeed USB.</text>
</plain>
